      "author_id": "61581601852251",
      "author_name": "Echoes of Unbound Curiosity",
      "message": "Time just broke, and it happened inside a dying star. Physicists ran the numbers on a collapsing neutron star and got something nobody saw coming. Time running in reverse. Not slowing down. Actually going backward. Everywhere else in the universe, time only moves one way. Eggs don't unscramble. Cold coffee doesn't warm itself back up. But push the equations into the chaos of a neutron star caving in on itself and that one-way street flips. It's math. Still, somewhere out there, a star collapsing into itself might be the one place the clock winds back.",
