      "post_id": "1149483064088104",
      "author_id": "100070792631636",
      "author_name": "Hypekage",
      "message": "Kikuko Inoue is one of the most recognizable veteran Japanese voice actresses in anime. She became especially famous as Kasumi Tendo in Ranma ½ and Belldandy in Ah! My Goddess, two performances that helped define her early career. Her résumé continued through major anime and game franchises. She voiced Sanae Furukawa in Clannad, Lust in Fullmetal Alchemist: Brotherhood, I-No in Guilty Gear, and Kirumi Tojo in Danganronpa V3: Killing Harmony. She has also appeared in numerous other anime, games, and dubbing projects. Inoue has remained active for decades while developing a particularly recognizable style for elegant, mature, and motherly characters. Her voice has consequently become familiar across romance, comedy, fantasy, action anime, and video games. Which Kikuko Inoue character introduced you to her voice: Belldandy, Kasumi, Sanae, Lust, or I-No? Happy 62nd birthday, Kikuko Inoue.",
